// GearSwap Atelier · module_catalog.js: the settings a player may want to change, by module, in the player's words.
// A module does one thing (Auto Medicine, the refill, the HUD...); the modules are ranged in groups by use (MOD_GROUPS).
// The Modules part (modules.js) shows these and only these in its simple view; every other setting of every file stays
// in its "All the files" view. Each entry names a settings file and a key of it, a title and what the setting does, in
// French and in English. The texts say what the file's own comments say (read 2026-10-11): when a comment changes,
// its entry here follows. A key the player's file does not hold is not shown.
//   file: its name ({JOB} = the job shown); key: the path in the file ({JOB}, {SUB} = the job and subjob shown)
//   cols: the setting is a table of lines (module_rows.js), {column: [kind, fr, en]}, kind 'slot', 'gear', 'item', 'num', 'count' (a number or 'all'), 'text'; gear: a list of pieces of equipment (icons)
//   range: [min, max, step] of a number (a unit in % is 0 to 100 by itself); std: its standard value; acts: a list of abilities and spells (picked in a window); rgb: a colour held as r, g, b
//   ws: a list of weaponskills (picked in a window, by the weapon's kind and the job); a key ending in `.*`: one option for each name under that table, said back as {1}
//   tip (a family): what the module does, said on its button and at the top of its options; use: how it is used in game; items: a list of game items (icons, picked in a window); bags: the bags a list may hold; unit: said after a number; only: the job the setting matters on; choices: [value, fr, en] for a closed choice
// (loaded before modules.js: see atelier/src/legacy/files.ts)

